# Tooltip and Popover Positioning

When a tooltip or popover is positioned with **`position: fixed`** and coordinates from **`getBoundingClientRect()`** (viewport coordinates), it **must** be rendered via **`createPortal(..., document.body)`**. Otherwise it will appear in the wrong place.

## Why

In CSS, any ancestor with `transform`, `perspective`, or `filter` creates a new **containing block** for `position: fixed` descendants. The fixed element is then positioned relative to that ancestor, not the viewport. We set `left`/`top` from viewport coordinates, so the element ends up mispositioned (e.g. "nowhere near" the trigger).

Common culprits: banner/panel `transform: translateY(...)`, modals, scroll containers with transform, or any animation wrapper.

## Rule

- **Do**: Render the tooltip/popover with `createPortal(content, document.body)` so it is a direct child of `body`. Then `position: fixed` is viewport-relative and viewport-based `left`/`top` are correct.
- **Don't**: Render the tooltip as a sibling or descendant of the trigger inside a transformed/stacking-context ancestor and rely on fixed + getBoundingClientRect().

## Example

```jsx
import { createPortal } from 'react-dom';

// ✅ CORRECT — tooltip in body, fixed position matches viewport coords
{tooltip && createPortal(
  <div
    className="fixed z-50 ..."
    style={{ left: tooltip.x, top: tooltip.y }}
  >
    {tooltip.content}
  </div>,
  document.body
)}
```

Existing examples in this repo: `CustomSelect.jsx` (option description tooltips), `Tooltip.jsx`, `DiceRoller.jsx` (Make a Scene / target menus), `GMTableView.jsx` (adversary target menu).
